# Grafana-Managed Alert Rule JSON Format

Based on the documentation, here's the complete JSON structure for creating a Grafana-managed alert rule via `POST /api/v1/provisioning/alert-rules`:

## Required Fields

```json
{
  "title": "string",
  "ruleGroup": "string",
  "folderUID": "string",
  "condition": "string",
  "data": [],
  "noDataState": "OK|NoData|AlertingKeepLastState",
  "execErrState": "OK|Alerting|AlertingKeepLastState",
  "for": "5m",
  "annotations": {},
  "labels": {}
}
```

## Complete Example with PromQL

```json
{
  "title": "High Quantile Latency",
  "ruleGroup": "Performance",
  "folderUID": "abc123xyz",
  "noDataState": "OK",
  "execErrState": "OK",
  "for": "5m",
  "condition": "B",
  "annotations": {
    "summary": "High p95 latency detected"
  },
  "labels": {
    "severity": "warning"
  },
  "data": [
    {
      "refId": "A",
      "queryType": "",
      "relativeTimeRange": {
        "from": 600,
        "to": 0
      },
      "datasourceUid": "prometheus-uid-here",
      "model": {
        "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, rate(request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m]))",
        "intervalMs": 1000,
        "maxDataPoints": 43200,
        "refId": "A"
      }
    },
    {
      "refId": "B",
      "queryType": "",
      "relativeTimeRange": {
        "from": 0,
        "to": 0
      },
      "datasourceUid": "-100",
      "model": {
        "conditions": [
          {
            "evaluator": {
              "params": [0.5],
              "type": "gt"
            },
            "operator": {
              "type": "and"
            },
            "query": {
              "params": ["A"]
            },
            "reducer": {
              "params": [],
              "type": "last"
            },
            "type": "query"
          }
        ],
        "datasource": {
          "type": "__expr__",
          "uid": "-100"
        },
        "refId": "B",
        "type": "classic_conditions"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Key Points

- **condition**: References a refId in the data array (typically an expression query)
- **datasourceUid**: Use actual datasource UID for queries; use `"-100"` for expression queries
- **model.expr**: Contains the PromQL query
- The condition field evaluates the query result against your threshold

